//*****************************************************************************
//  AIOF.ohf  --  ALL-IN or FOLD  (a complete, self-contained push/fold profile)
//
//  Every preflop decision is RaiseMax (jam the whole stack) or Fold. No limping,
//  no flat-calling, no sized raises. Built for hyper-turbo / spin&go / very short
//  stacks, and as a clean Nash-style push/fold base you can tune.
//
//  Engine conventions (matches the ScarletBeast tree):
//    - StackSize and bet symbols are in BIG BLINDS.
//    - Hand-range LISTS are ##named## (hands spelled out) and referenced bare.
//    - All-in == RaiseMax.  OpenPPL has NO not-equal operator (use ==, >=, <=, NOT).
//
//  Width scales with effective stack depth and position; tighter when facing a
//  raise (reshove). Above ~25bb it stops open-jamming (deep AIOF is -EV) and folds.
//  Postflop never voluntarily invests (you are all-in or folded before the flop).
//
//  TUNING: widen / tighten purely by editing the ##listShove*## / ##listReshove*##
//  blocks. The decision logic never needs to change.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$preflop##
// Scrape-safety gate: on a HARD mis-scrape, never jam the stack on garbage data.
// Take the free check if there is one, otherwise fold. (validator_ok is engine-native.)
WHEN validator_ok == 0 AND AmountToCall == 0 Check FORCE
WHEN validator_ok == 0 Fold FORCE
// Facing a raise / 3-bet -> re-shove a value range, else fold.
WHEN Raises >= 1 RETURN f$AIOF_Reshove FORCE
// Unopened or limped to us -> open-shove by stack depth x position.
WHEN Raises == 0 RETURN f$AIOF_Open FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Open-shove (folded / limped to us): late position (CO/BTN/SB heads-up) jams
//  wider than early/middle at every depth. >25bb: stop open-jamming, fold.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
##f$AIOF_Open##
// Never fold the nut tier, at ANY depth -- freeroll fields are loose and pay off jams.
WHEN listAlwaysJam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN f$AIOF_Late AND StackSize <= 7  AND listShove75 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN f$AIOF_Late AND StackSize <= 12 AND listShove50 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN f$AIOF_Late AND StackSize <= 18 AND listShove30 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN f$AIOF_Late AND StackSize <= 25 AND listShove15 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 7  AND listShove50 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 12 AND listShove30 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 18 AND listShove15 RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 25 AND listShovePremium RaiseMax FORCE
// Free option in the big blind: take the check, never fold for free.
WHEN InBigBlind AND AmountToCall == 0 Check FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Reshove (call-off all-in over a raise): value-weighted, widening when shorter.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
##f$AIOF_Reshove##
// Re-jam the nut tier over any raise, at any depth.
WHEN listAlwaysJam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 10 AND listReshoveWide  RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 16 AND listReshoveMid   RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN StackSize <= 22 AND listReshoveTight RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

// "Late" = cutoff, button, the late seat, or the small blind (heads-up vs the BB).
##f$AIOF_Late##
WHEN InLatePosition OR InCutOff OR InButton OR InSmallBlind RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  SHOVE RANGES (open).  ~75 / 50 / 30 / 15 / 8 percent of hands.
//=============================================================================
##listAlwaysJam##
// Get-it-in at ANY depth -- the tier you never fold, even deep.
AA KK QQ JJ AKs AKo

##listShove75##
// ultra-short late jam (~75%)
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
A2o A3o A4o A5o A6o A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo
K2s K3s K4s K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs
K5o K6o K7o K8o K9o KTo KJo KQo
Q4s Q5s Q6s Q7s Q8s Q9s QTs QJs
Q8o Q9o QTo QJo
J6s J7s J8s J9s JTs
J8o J9o JTo
T6s T7s T8s T9s
T8o T9o
96s 97s 98s
97o 98o
85s 86s 87s
86o 87o
74s 75s 76s
64s 65s
53s 54s
43s

##listShove50##
// short jam (~50%)
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
A4o A5o A6o A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo
K4s K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs
K8o K9o KTo KJo KQo
Q7s Q8s Q9s QTs QJs
