##listShove15##
// tight jam (~15%)
44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
ATo AJo AQo AKo
KTs KJs KQs
KJo KQo
QJs

##listShovePremium##
// nut-only jam (~8%) -- used when deeper than ideal for AIOF
88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
AQs AKs
AKo

//=============================================================================
//  RESHOVE RANGES (re-jam over a raise).  value-weighted.
//=============================================================================
##listReshoveWide##
// <=10bb call-off (~22%)
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo
KTs KJs KQs
KJo KQo
QJs

##listReshoveMid##
// <=16bb call-off (~12%)
55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
AJo AQo AKo
KQs

##listReshoveTight##
// <=22bb call-off (~7%)
88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
AJs AQs AKs
AQo AKo
KQs

//=============================================================================
//  POSTFLOP -- safety net only. An AIOF bot is all-in or folded preflop, so it
//  should never reach a postflop decision with chips behind. Never invest here.
//=============================================================================
##f$flop##
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 Check FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

##f$turn##
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 Check FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

##f$river##
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 Check FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE
